WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.700
Pixar loves to load its animated movies with
easter eggs and hidden details and there are

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.870
stacks of them you might have missed when
you first watched Cars 3.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:13.469
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and with Cars 3 available now to watch at

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:17.180
home, I've gone through the movie with a fine
toothcomb and today I'll be explaining all

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.140
the Pixar easter eggs and cool details hidden
in the film.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:25.090
Also, I'm starting a new Disney Funko giveaway
for one of these Cars pop figures.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.010
For a chance to win, make sure you're subscribed
to my channel and leave me a comment about

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.990
your favourite easter eggs you spotted in
the movie.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:35.840
And just a quick warning before we start,
I'll be discussing spoilers from Cars 3, so

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.890
take care if you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.379
Cruz's license plate is a clever shout-out
to the actress Cristela Alonzo who voices

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:47.360
the character in the movie.
It's a combination of her initials, C and

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.109
A, and then her birthday January 6th.
Plus the plate is registered in Texgas, a

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:56.379
pun on Texas, which is where Alonzo was born.

00:00:56.379 --> 00:01:01.809
The Sleep Well motel from Toy Story of Terror
also shows up in Cars 3 on a giant roadside

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:05.770
advert above the bridge where Mack and Lightning
spend the night after the Thunder Hollow incident.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.479
The sign says "Time To Re-Tire?" which reflects
Lightning's state of mind at that moment as

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:15.560
he's just had an argument with Cruz after
she won the demolition derby and he's thinking

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.780
about giving up racing for good.
But it's also an extra reference to Toy Story

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.090
of Terror and how Bonnie's mom had to stay
at the Sleep Well motel after she got a flat

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.200
tyre.
Also on that billboard, there's a deep-cut

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:34.259
easter egg to Pixar's incorporation date in
the numbers 0-2-0-3-86, in other words, February

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:37.670
3rd, 1986.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.570
And while Mack is sleeping below the bridge,
inside Lightning is flipping channels, and,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:47.210
for just a moment, the Cars 2 scene of a kissing
couple on the Pont des Arts in Paris pops

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.110
up on the TV screen.
By the way, those kissing cars are named John

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:55.640
and Nancy after Pixar's John Lasseter and
his wife, whose favourite colour just happens

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.409
to be lavender, the same as the female car
in the scene.

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:04.909
One of the most memorable moments in Cars
3 is the demolition derby race where we meet

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:08.320
the fearsome Miss Fritter.
And the scenes at the Thunder Hollow Speedway

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.110
are also a fantastic treasure trove of Pixar
easter eggs and references for fans to appreciate.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:18.380
During the contest, one of the competitors,
Bill, gets pushed along by Miss Fritter and

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:23.701
his colour design is the same as Pixar's famous
Luxo ball, plus he even has the Luxo ball

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:27.710
painted on his hood.
The Luxo ball appeared in Pixar's very first

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:33.170
short film, Luxo Jr together with two desk
lamps, one of which is still used in Pixar's

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.440
logo.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.120
Another competitor at the Thunder Hollow demolition
derby is the Pizza Planet Truck, aka Todd,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.100
who has appeared in both of the previous two
Cars movies, and in Cars 3 at one point a

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.610
car goes crashing into him which knocks the
Pizza Planet rocket off his roof and sends

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.750
it flying into the crowd.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:56.250
A Crazy Eight racer called T-Bone, whose body
is kind of twisted, has a street sign at the

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.170
front of his hood in the race.
The sign reads Park Avenue, a shout-out to

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:05.340
the location of Pixar Animation Studios' main
office at 1200 Park Ave, Emeryville.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.460
Miss Fritter is, of course, the queen of the
track at Thunder Hollow and the design of

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.590
her smokestacks are a deliberate homage to
the horns of the classic Disney villain Maleficent.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:20.310
And dotted around the speedway are a number
of billboards which have some super-sneaky

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.740
easter eggs hidden within them.
There's a car life insurance ad by a company

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:31.150
called Insuricare which is the same insurance
company that Bob works for in The Incredibles.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.940
And the Wild Bill's Racing Cones billboard
is a reference to Cars 3 production designer

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.090
Bill Cone.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:42.980
And the radio station "Wild 86.2 FM" is another
deep cut easter egg to the month and year

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:48.890
when Pixar was incorporated, February 1986.
By the way, there's yet another nod to that

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:54.760
year in the movie as the number of Bill, the
Luxo Ball car, is 86, and 1986 is also the

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:00.500
year that Pixar released their first short
film, Luxo Jr., which also featured the Luxo

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.500
Ball.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:06.260
In 1986, it was Steve Jobs who provided the
investment money for Pixar's spin-out as a

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:11.560
corporation from Lucasfilm, and since then
Pixar have included numerous homages in their

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.280
movies to Steve Jobs' most famous brand, Apple.
In Cars 3, you can hear the Mac starting sound

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:23.590
when Cruz boots up the treadmill on Fireball
Beach.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:27.970
You might also have heard the same sound in
WALL-E as it plays after WALL-E has finished

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.950
charging himself.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:40.610
Speaking of WALL-E, there's an easter egg
to that movie via the BnL, aka Buy n Large,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.370
track sponsor at one of the speedways.
BnL is the corporation in WALL•E that basically

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:49.220
enabled the pollution of the planet and sent
humans away from Earth while it attempted

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:53.210
to clear it up.
A BnL Raceway logo also appears during the

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.970
Cars 3 credits.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:00.140
Pixar's films always include easter eggs for
their next movie, which in the case of Cars

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.570
3 means Coco.
And there are loads of Coco easter eggs and

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.210
references in this Cars 3.
For example, you can spot the guitar from

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.940
Coco on the stage behind Sweet Tea and her
band at the Cotter Pin bar.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:16.670
The town where Coco is set, Santa Cecilia,
appears on the treadmill screen at the Rust-eze

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:20.890
Racing Center when one of the homesick cars
thinks of home.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:24.990
And there's also a neat Coco-inspired brand
of liquor in the bar where Miss Fritter and

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:30.230
her friends go to watch the Florida 500 race.
The brand advertised is torquela which is

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.980
a clever car-based pun on torque and tequila.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:39.060
While Miss Fritter's in that bar, you'll need
to look very carefully to spot a sneaky A-1-1-3

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:44.020
easter egg via one of the license plates hanging
on the side of the school bus, and you can

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:48.250
see that a bit more clearly during the Crazy
Eight demolition derby as well.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:52.410
Miss Fritter collects license plates from
the opponents she defeats at the Thunder Hollow

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.020
speedway and she also seems to collect street
signs.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:59.150
And one of those street signs is for "West
Cutting Boulevard", a reference to the street

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:03.639
address of Pixar's former headquarters in
Richmond, California.

00:06:03.639 --> 00:06:08.750
Other Cars 3 A-1-1-3 easter eggs include one
on the press sticker that track reporter Shannon

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:12.760
Spokes wears on her side.
And there's a fairly obvious A-1-1-3 on the

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:16.300
door to Sterling's office at the Rust-eze
Racing Centre.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.470
And inside Sterling's office, there are some
more cool easter eggs.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:24.470
Hidden among the trophies on his shelves is
Cinderella's pumpkin carriage.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:28.730
The movie's set department included this as
it's a four-wheeled vehicle and is a fun little

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.950
nod to one of Disney's classic films.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.620
And this one is much harder to see, but if
you look very carefully, there's a small picture

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.730
of Sir Miles Axlerod, the villain from Cars
2, which might suggest that Sterling once

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:45.700
knew the evil mastermind from the second Cars
movie.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:50.389
The miniature tree on Sterling's desk also
looks a lot like the tree from A Bug's Life

00:06:50.389 --> 00:06:54.220
which has also appeared previously in Up and
Toy Story 2.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:59.610
And before Lightning went to the Rust-eze
Racing Centre, he spoke on a payphone to Rusty

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:04.280
and Dusty from Radiator Springs.
Now, that payphone was originally designed

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.340
to appear in the first Cars movie but ended
up being cut.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:14.210
In fact, when Cars 3 production designer Jay
Shuster joined Pixar back in the early 2000s,

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:18.870
that payphone was one of the very first things
he created.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:23.830
During the Florida 500 race, one of racers
spins out of control nearly causing a multiple

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:27.900
car accident.
The spinning car is number 31 and its sponsor

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.419
is Triple Dent Gum, which is the chewing gum
from Inside Out that had a recurring jingle

00:07:32.419 --> 00:07:34.520
that played throughout that movie.

